-- title:
--   Proposition 3.8: Four equivalent tests in a simple hermitian algebra
-- statement:
--   All vector spaces and Lie algebras are finite dimensional and real, with their usual Hausdorff topology. An invariant set is invariant under the group generated by $e^{\operatorname{ad}y}$. A closed convex set is pointed when its recession edge is zero. Write $\mathcal O_x=\operatorname{Inn}(\mathfrak g)x$, $\operatorname{co}(x)=\overline{\operatorname{conv}}\mathcal O_x$, and $C_x=\operatorname{cone}(\mathcal O_x)$. Admissibility means existence of a pointed generating invariant closed convex subset.
--
--   Let $\mathfrak g$ be simple hermitian, $x=x_s+x_n$ its commuting ad-semisimple/ad-nilpotent Jordan decomposition, and $W_{\max}$ a maximal pointed invariant cone. The following four conditions are equivalent:
--
--   $$C_x\text{ pointed};\quad C_{x_s},C_{x_n}\text{ pointed and }(x_s\ne0\Rightarrow x_n\in C_{x_s});\quad x\in W_{\max}\cup(-W_{\max});\quad\operatorname{co}(x)\text{ pointed}.$$
--
--   Under these equivalent conditions, $x_s\ne0$ implies $C_x=C_{x_s}$. The last identity is scoped as in the source proof. This characterizes pointedness in the simple hermitian case.
-- source:
--   Elements in pointed invariant cones in Lie algebras and corresponding affine pairs, arXiv:2110.07297v1, PDF p. 9, Proposition 3.8: Four equivalent tests in a simple hermitian algebra

